id: DRAFT-rset-3.3-toybox-awk-script-args
category: compat, platform, shell
build_system: shell|runtime
phase: runtime
match_keywords: awk, toybox awk, Unknown option, renv, -f /dev/fd/3, shebang, script arguments, polyglot, heredoc
error_signature: "awk: Unknown option 'q' (see \"awk --help\") when running '#!/usr/bin/awk -f' scripts with dash-prefixed script arguments"
error_excerpt: "renv - -q fails with 'awk: Unknown option q' under toybox awk; the same script works under gawk"
root_cause: "toybox 0.8.12 awk violates POSIX argument parsing: after the first operand it still parses dash-prefixed arguments as awk's own options instead of passing them to the script's ARGV. Upstream awk scripts with shebang '#!/usr/bin/awk -f' that accept flags like -q silently break on OHOS. env -S is unavailable so shebang tricks don't help."
rec_approach: "Convert the awk script into a single-file sh+awk polyglot: shebang #!/bin/sh, then 'exec awk -f /dev/fd/3 -- \"$@\" 3<<'QUOTED_EOF'' followed by the original awk program body and the terminator line. The '--' stops option parsing so dash-prefixed script arguments reach ARGV untouched; quoting the heredoc delimiter prevents shell expansion of the program body (important for scripts emitting \\$ escapes); keeping everything in one file preserves rset's remote-staging distribution model (rset copies renv to the target host as a single file)."
solution: "See archives/r/rset/3.3/patches/0001-renv.awk.patch (rset 3.3): renv.awk converted to sh+awk polyglot. Upstream test_renv.rb went from 6/7 to 7/7; conan test_package verifies 'renv - -q' prints errors only. Works unchanged under gawk/mawk on GNU/Linux."
fallback: "If the target platform lacks /dev/fd, fall back to writing the program body to a mktemp file and 'trap rm' cleanup; still keep -- before script arguments."
prescan_pattern: "#!/usr/bin/awk -f"
verify_builds: "rset 3.3 local conan create (ohos-aarch64): test_package all green; upstream Ruby suite 37/40 (remaining 3 failures are E046 chmod, unrelated)"
severity: 2
last_updated: 2026-10-03
